# Copy to .env for local development.
#
# The two Supabase values come from Supabase › Project Settings › API. The anon
# key is a public client key: it is compiled into the JS bundle and anyone can
# read it. That is fine — Row-Level Security is the actual boundary, and the anon
# key on its own grants nothing until a user signs in. Never put the service_role
# key here; it belongs only in the edge function's environment.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# OPTIONAL. Leave blank unless you are rotating the VAPID keypair or pointing a
# build at a second Supabase project.
#
# This is the PUBLIC half of the Web Push keypair — the identity a browser hands
# its push service at subscribe time, so it ships in the bundle by design and is
# not a secret. Blank is the normal case: src/lib/push.ts carries the current key
# as DEFAULT_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY and falls back to it, which is why push works on
# GitHub Pages whether or not this variable is set.
#
# When it IS set, Vite inlines it and drops the constant from the bundle
# altogether — that is what makes a rotation a secret change rather than a code
# change. It must equal the `VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY` function secret on `send-push`, or
# every subscription made against this build is undeliverable. See
# docs/RUNBOOK.md §4.2.
VITE_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=
